  "confounds": {
    "atlas_scope": "Head-ganglia neurons only (168 stimulated neurons, Fig 2a WT n=113 animals). Ventral-cord motor classes are represented ONLY by their head-most members: VA: ['VA1']; VB: ['VB1', 'VB2']; DA: ['DA1']; DB: ['DB2']; VD: NONE; DD: ['DD1']. VD has zero measured members and is untestable. The motor-class comparison is therefore built on 1-2 anterior members per class and is NOT a fair test of the model's ventral-cord claims; the restricted sensory/interneuron test (n=8) is the primary one.",
    "background": "Wild-type dataset used (Fig 2a). unc-31 dataset (ED Fig 7) exists but not used.",
    "directionality": "Model perturbation = chronic cell-autonomous leak-conductance change; atlas = acute optogenetic stimulation. Related but not identical quantities.",
    "stimulation_efficacy": "Per-class coverage (n_measured_out) reported; count-based metrics are coverage-normalised (sig_fraction). Stimulation efficacy per neuron class (opsin expression, autoresponse amplitude) not controlled here.",
    "model_side_limitation": "B6b JSON stores only ordered top-4 stiffest-class lists per condition, not continuous per-class curvature; model load is ordinal (4..1, else 0), heavily tied. BAAI_chemo gives only group-level (chemo-group vs motor-group) sensitivities, not per-class values."
